            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0321" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Taipei</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Edgar</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-10T09:00:00+08:00">April 10, 1949—9
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 10—2:14 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. [For] Merchant and Butterworth. T. V. Soong here. He tells me on
                    Generalissimo’s order to find political, economic, military solution to preclude
                    Communist takeover. Asked my advice. Have stalled. You may decide immediate
                    return or request my instructions.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 108, repeated Nanking 98.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edgar</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
